cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "BioChirp: Federated Biomedical Retrieval with Provenance and MCP Integration"
message: "If you use BioChirp in research, please cite this software and the accompanying paper."
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-05-10
authors:
 - family-names: Gupta
 given-names: Abhishekh
 affiliation: "Indraprastha Institute of Information Technology Delhi (IIIT-Delhi)"
 email: abhishekh@iiitd.ac.in
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/abhishekhgupta/biochirp"
url: "https://biochirp.iiitd.edu.in"
abstract: >-
 BioChirp federates 26 curated biomedical databases (BioGRID, STRING,
 OmniPath, Orphanet, ChEMBL, ClinVar, HPO, Reactome,
 WikiPathways, MSigDB, DGIdb, DrugCentral, TTD, PharmGKB, HGNC, …) into a
 unified retrieval interface. Every row carries (db_version,
 db_snapshot_date) provenance. The system exposes 29 Model Context Protocol
 servers (1 federation + 28 per-database) totalling 72 tools, and includes a
 token-budget-aware retrieval planner formalised as a Multiple-Choice
 Knapsack with priorities (NP-hard; greedy empirical competitive ratio
 0.9998). Distributed as a PyPI package, a Claude Desktop DXT bundle, and
 a hosted HTTP/SSE endpoint.
keywords:
 - biomedical retrieval
 - knowledge graph
